Lemma 5: f(f(X, f(f(Y, Z), f(Y, Z))), f(f(f(f(Z, f(Z, Z)), X), f(Y, Z)), X)) = f(Y, Z).
Proof:
  f(f(X, f(f(Y, Z), f(Y, Z))), f(f(f(f(Z, f(Z, Z)), X), f(Y, Z)), X))
= { by axiom 1 (hyp) }
  f(f(X, f(f(Y, Z), f(Y, f(f(Z, f(Z, Z)), f(f(f(W, Z), f(V, f(Z, W))), Z))))), f(f(f(f(Z, f(Z, Z)), X), f(Y, Z)), X))
